# polygons, axes, grid, and saving and loading a screen within one run
GI
# filled triangle: inside, outside, a vertex and a point on the slanted edge
K 3:PV 10 10:PV 30 10:PV 10 30:PF
!pixel 0 15 15 3
!pixel 0 25 25 0
!pixel 0 30 10 3
!pixel 0 20 20 3
# outline only
K 4:PV 100 100:PV 120 100:PV 120 120:PV 100 120:PO
!pixel 0 110 100 4
!pixel 0 110 110 0
!pixel 0 120 110 4
PF
!err 2
PV 1 1:PO
!err 2
# at most 64 vertices; the list survives across lines
PV 0 200
PV 1 200
PV 2 200
PV 3 200
PV 4 200
PV 5 200
PV 6 200
PV 7 200
PV 8 200
PV 9 200
PV 10 200
PV 11 200
PV 12 200
PV 13 200
PV 14 200
PV 15 200
PV 16 200
PV 17 200
PV 18 200
PV 19 200
PV 20 200
PV 21 200
PV 22 200
PV 23 200
PV 24 200
PV 25 200
PV 26 200
PV 27 200
PV 28 200
PV 29 200
PV 30 200
PV 31 200
PV 32 200
PV 33 200
PV 34 200
PV 35 200
PV 36 200
PV 37 200
PV 38 200
PV 39 200
PV 40 200
PV 41 200
PV 42 200
PV 43 200
PV 44 200
PV 45 200
PV 46 200
PV 47 200
PV 48 200
PV 49 200
PV 50 200
PV 51 200
PV 52 200
PV 53 200
PV 54 200
PV 55 200
PV 56 200
PV 57 200
PV 58 200
PV 59 200
PV 60 200
PV 61 200
PV 62 200
PV 63 200
PV 70 200
!err 4
PO
!err 0
# axes through the user origin with ticks
GI:SX -10 10:SY -10 10:K 7:AX 5 5
!pixel 0 0 160 7
!pixel 0 479 160 7
!pixel 0 240 0 7
!pixel 0 240 319 7
!pixel 0 359 157 7
!pixel 0 359 156 0
!pixel 0 237 80 7
!pixel 0 236 80 0
# grid lines every 5 user units
GI:SX 0 10:SY 0 10:K 9:GR 5 5
!pixel 0 240 50 9
!pixel 0 241 50 0
!pixel 0 50 160 9
!pixel 0 50 161 0
!pixel 0 0 50 9
!pixel 0 479 50 9
GR -1 1
!err 4
# save the target screen, load it into another
GI:T 2:C 9:W 5 5 3:KP 9 1 2 3:VS TESTSCR
!err 0
T 3:VL TESTSCR
!pixel 3 5 5 3
!pixel 3 6 6 9
?P 9
!reply 1 2 3
VL NOSUCHSCR
!err 8
VS BAD/NAME
!err 8
?E
!reply E 8 NO FILE
